		<title type="html"><![CDATA[User postgres]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=27642#p27642"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,<br />J&#039;ai installé la version 10 on Linux.<br />Suivant la page: <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/download/linux/redhat/" rel="nofollow">https://www.postgresql.org/download/linux/redhat/</a></p><p>Je constate que l&#039;utilisateur postgres existe :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>[root@rac1 ~]# ps -ef | grep postgres
postgres  3221     1  0 15:35 ?        00:00:00 /usr/pgsql-10/bin/postmaster -D /var/lib/pgsql/10/data
postgres  3223  3221  0 15:35 ?        00:00:00 postgres: logger process                              
postgres  3225  3221  0 15:35 ?        00:00:00 postgres: checkpointer process                        
postgres  3226  3221  0 15:35 ?        00:00:00 postgres: writer process                              
postgres  3227  3221  0 15:35 ?        00:00:00 postgres: wal writer process                          
postgres  3228  3221  0 15:35 ?        00:00:05 postgres: autovacuum launcher process                 
postgres  3229  3221  0 15:35 ?        00:00:00 postgres: stats collector process                     
postgres  3230  3221  0 15:35 ?        00:00:00 postgres: bgworker: logical replication launcher      
root      7157  7002  0 17:14 pts/0    00:00:00 grep postgres</code></pre></div><br /><p>Mais il n&#039;a pas de répertoire home:</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>[root@rac1 ~]# ls -l /home
total 8
drwx------. 22 oracle oinstall 4096 May 24 16:44 oracle
[root@rac1 ~]#</code></pre></div><p>Comment l&#039;expliquer?</p><p>Quand je me connecte à Linux avec le compte postgres :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>bash-4.1$ id
uid=26(postgres) gid=26(postgres) groups=26(postgres)
bash-4.1$ pwd
/var/lib/pgsql
bash-4.1$ </code></pre></div><p>Dois-je corriger? Que faire?</p><p>D&#039;avance merci.</p>]]></content>
